stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> IN_SERVICE
    IN_SERVICE --> NOTICED: M1 provider publishes a deprecation notice and the dates are captured
    IN_SERVICE --> SUSPENDED: M7 provider suspends the configuration with no notice
    NOTICED --> CANDIDATE_EVAL: M2 successor candidates listed from the cohort eligible set
    CANDIDATE_EVAL --> MIGRATION_SCHEDULED: M3 a candidate passes parity and has a published price row
    CANDIDATE_EVAL --> BLOCKED: M4 no candidate passes parity or none is in the consented set
    BLOCKED --> CANDIDATE_EVAL: M5 eligibility, consent or parity record changes
    MIGRATION_SCHEDULED --> MIGRATED: M6 tier map re-pointed before the retirement date
    MIGRATION_SCHEDULED --> RETIRED_UNMIGRATED: M8 retirement date reached with the migration incomplete
    BLOCKED --> RETIRED_UNMIGRATED: M8 retirement date reached with no successor
    SUSPENDED --> MIGRATED: M9 the in-tier fallback becomes the default once parity is current
    RETIRED_UNMIGRATED --> MIGRATED: M10 a successor clears parity and eligibility later
    MIGRATED --> [*]

    note right of RETIRED_UNMIGRATED
        The class takes its degraded path.
        Never a cross-tier promotion, never a
        provider outside the tenant eligible set.
    end note

    note left of CANDIDATE_EVAL
        Quality first for any class whose output
        feeds a statutory artefact. Cost deltas
        come from the per-event matrix at the
        rate in force.
    end note
